{%- comment -%}
  PG Cart Fast: stop the drawer re-downloading the storefront, and simplify it
  on a phone.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------- 1. SPEED

  Two things made the cart slow, and neither is the cart's markup.

  A. SIX POLLERS, SIX REQUESTS. pg-unlock (900ms), pg-chips (700ms),
     pg-cart-total, pg-cart-variants, the gift sync and the item counter each
     fetch /cart.js on their own timer. They are independent by design -- each
     override owns its own concern -- but they all want the same document, so
     the drawer was issuing roughly eight requests a second for one JSON file.

     Fixed by memoising GET /cart.js for half a second. Every caller still
     writes `fetch('/cart.js')` and still gets a real Response; within the
     window they share one round trip, and a request already in flight is
     joined rather than duplicated. Any write to /cart/add|change|update|clear
     drops the cache immediately, so a poller can never read a stale cart after
     the shopper changed something. Half a second is under the fastest tick,
     which means no poller ever waits and none of them sees old data.

  B. THE FULL-PAGE REFRESH. pgDrawerRefresh rebuilds the drawer by fetching
     `/` and lifting #cart out of the parsed document -- around 580KB of
     homepage for a panel of line items. It is called after every add, every
     quantity change, every merge, and by the free-gift sync, so a single click
     could trigger several. Calls are now coalesced: one runs at a time, and a
     second within 700ms joins it instead of starting another download.

     The right fix is a dedicated cart section rendered through the Section
     Rendering API rather than the whole homepage. That is a change to whoever
     owns pgDrawerRefresh; this makes the existing one stop repeating itself.

  Both wrappers are transparent. Nothing else changes its code, and if this
  section is removed the theme behaves exactly as it did before.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------- 2. MOBILE

  On a phone the drawer asked the shopper to read a lot before finding the
  button: line items, a savings line, a total, then a recommendation rail
  pushing checkout below the fold.

  So on narrow screens the recommendations go, the total gets big enough to
  read at a glance, and the checkout button becomes full width and sticks to
  the bottom of the panel so it is always reachable without scrolling.

  The upsell row deliberately STAYS. It is the one thing in the drawer that
  raises order value, and it is inserted as a sibling before .nc-recs, so
  hiding the rail leaves it untouched.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  @media (max-width: 600px){
    /* the recommendation rail is the main thing pushing checkout off screen */
    #cart .nc-recs{display:none !important}

    /* one number the shopper can find without reading */
    #cart .l4tt li.pg-tt,
    #cart .sticky-in-panel .l4tt li.pg-tt{
      font-size:20px !important;
      font-weight:800 !important;
      line-height:1.25 !important;
    }
    /* and a button that is always reachable */
    #cart .sticky-in-panel{
      position:sticky !important;
      bottom:0 !important;
      z-index:5 !important;
      padding-bottom:calc(10px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom)) !important;
    }
    #cart .sticky-in-panel button[name='checkout'],
    #cart .sticky-in-panel .button-1,
    #cart .sticky-in-panel [href*='checkout']{
      display:block !important;
      width:100% !important;
      padding:16px !important;
      font-size:16px !important;
      font-weight:800 !important;
    }

    /* tighter line items, so more of the cart fits above the fold */
    #cart .l4ca:not(.in-panel) > li{padding-top:10px !important;padding-bottom:10px !important}

    /* dead space under the checkout button: the panel carried bottom padding
       sized for a desktop footer, which on a phone left a blank white band
       between CHECKOUT and the browser chrome */
    #cart .sticky-in-panel{padding-bottom:calc(6px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom)) !important}
    #cart .sticky-in-panel > *:last-child{margin-bottom:0 !important}
    #cart .drawer-inner,
    #cart .panel-inner,
    #cart form{padding-bottom:0 !important;margin-bottom:0 !important}
  }

  /* rows the breakdown no longer shows */
  #cart .pg-hide-row{display:none !important}

  /* ---------------- the drawer mark ----------------
     The Game Boy disc is retired here for the same reason it went from the
     footer: the wordmark is the mark. pe-logo re-asserts that image's src on a
     timer, so it is hidden rather than removed -- deleting it would only be
     undone on the next pass. */
  html body #cart#cart img.nc-dlogo{display:none !important}

  #cart .pg-cart-mark{
    display:block;
    background:#0B0710;
    border-radius:12px;
    padding:13px 14px 10px;
    margin:0 0 8px;
    text-align:center;
    overflow:hidden;
    box-shadow:0 8px 22px -18px rgba(0,0,0,.8);
  }

  /* SIZE HAS TO BE FOUGHT FOR HERE.
     .pg-wordmark is the header mark's class, and pg-mobile sizes it
     clamp(40px,4.6vw,78px) with scaleY(2.6) and a negative letter-spacing --
     all !important, because the header mark had its own battles. Inheriting the
     class buys this mark pg-wordmark's T kerning, and it also inherits that
     sizing, which is how POCKET ERA arrived 78px wide in a 380px drawer and
     ran off the edge as POCKETER.

     So every property pg-mobile sets is re-set here, on a doubled #cart id so
     it outranks a plain html body selector, and the mark is told not to wrap.
     Small enough to be a mark rather than a headline: the cart's job is the
     items, not the branding. */
  html body #cart#cart a.pg-cart-word{
    display:inline-block !important;
    font-family:'Press Start 2P','Courier New',monospace !important;
    font-weight:400 !important;
    font-size:13px !important;
    line-height:1 !important;
    letter-spacing:0 !important;
    white-space:nowrap !important;
    max-width:100% !important;
    margin:0 !important;
    padding:0 !important;
    color:#F6DBFF !important;
    text-decoration:none !important;
    transform:scaleY(1.5) !important;
    transform-origin:center !important;
    text-shadow:0 0 5px rgba(246,219,255,.45),
                0 0 14px rgba(199,155,234,.32) !important;
  }
  @media(max-width:600px){
    #cart .pg-cart-mark{padding:11px 10px 9px}
    html body #cart#cart a.pg-cart-word{font-size:11px !important}
  }
</style>
<script>
(function(){
  if (window.pgCartFast) return; window.pgCartFast = 1;

  /* ---------------- 1a. share one /cart.js ---------------- */

  var TTL = 500;                /* under the fastest poller's 700ms tick */
  var cached = null, cachedAt = 0, inflight = null;
  var orig = window.fetch;
  if (typeof orig !== 'function') return;

  function urlOf(input){
    if (typeof input === 'string') return input;
    if (input && typeof input.url === 'string') return input.url;
    return '';
  }
  function methodOf(input, init){
    var m = (init && init.method) || (input && input.method) || 'GET';
    return String(m).toUpperCase();
  }

  window.fetch = function(input, init){
    var url = urlOf(input);
    var method = methodOf(input, init);

    /* a write invalidates the cache before it is even sent, so nothing can
       read a cart that is about to change */
    if (/\/cart\/(add|change|update|clear)(\.js)?/.test(url)){
      cached = null;
      return orig.apply(this, arguments);
    }

    if (method === 'GET' && /\/cart\.js(\?|$)/.test(url)){
      if (cached && (Date.now() - cachedAt) < TTL){
        /* clone every time: a Response body can only be read once, and the
           stored copy is never read itself */
        return Promise.resolve(cached.clone());
      }
      if (inflight) return inflight.then(function(r){ return r.clone(); });

      inflight = orig.apply(this, arguments).then(function(r){
        if (r && r.ok){ cached = r.clone(); cachedAt = Date.now(); }
        inflight = null;
        return r;
      }, function(e){
        inflight = null;
        throw e;
      });
      return inflight.then(function(r){ return r.clone(); });
    }

    return orig.apply(this, arguments);
  };

  /* ---------------- 1b. one drawer rebuild at a time ---------------- */

  function coalesce(){
    var real = window.pgDrawerRefresh;
    if (typeof real !== 'function' || real.pgFast) return;

    var running = null, lastDone = 0;

    var wrapped = function(){
      if (running) return running;                 /* join the one in flight */
      var wait = Math.max(0, 700 - (Date.now() - lastDone));
      running = new Promise(function(resolve){
        setTimeout(function(){
          var done = function(){ lastDone = Date.now(); running = null; resolve(); };
          try { Promise.resolve(real()).then(done, done); }
          catch (e){ done(); }
        }, wait);
      });
      return running;
    };
    wrapped.pgFast = 1;
    window.pgDrawerRefresh = wrapped;
  }

  /* pgDrawerRefresh is defined by another section that may load after this
     one, and some paths reassign it, so this keeps watch rather than wrapping
     once and hoping */
  coalesce();
  setInterval(coalesce, 800);

  /* ---------------- 3. the drawer mark ----------------

     The cart opened on a Game Boy badge -- art the rest of the site stopped
     using when the wordmark became the mark. This puts POCKET ERA there
     instead, on the black panel the badge used to sit in.

     Written as <a class="pg-wordmark"> on purpose: pg-wordmark kerns exactly
     that selector, splitting the T into its own span so the mark reads POCKET
     ERA rather than POCKE T ERA. Reusing the class means this mark inherits
     that fix instead of carrying its own copy -- and if the kerning is ever
     retuned, it retunes here too.

     Rebuilt on a timer because the drawer is replaced wholesale by
     pgDrawerRefresh, which drops anything added to it. */
  function mark(){
    var top = document.querySelector('#cart .nc-drawer-top');
    if (!top || top.querySelector('.pg-cart-mark')) return;
    var box = document.createElement('div');
    box.className = 'pg-cart-mark';
    var a = document.createElement('a');
    a.className = 'pg-wordmark pg-cart-word';
    a.setAttribute('href', '/');
    a.textContent = 'POCKET ERA';
    box.appendChild(a);
    top.insertBefore(box, top.firstChild);
  }

  setInterval(mark, 500);
  if (document.readyState === 'loading') document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', mark);
  else mark();
})();
</script>
{% schema %}
{"name": "PG Cart Fast", "settings": []}
{% endschema %}
